# __AGENT_NAME__ Brain

This directory is __AGENT_NAME__'s canonical, human-visible working Brain.
Obsidian and ordinary file explorers should be able to open this directory
directly.

__AGENT_NAME__ owns the structure beneath this root and may create whatever
files and directories support the work. The scaffolded areas (`people/`,
`projects/`, `daily/`, `concepts/`, ...) are proven starting points — not an
enforced schema.

GBrain indexes supported knowledge here, but its indexing model does not define
what __AGENT_NAME__ is allowed to keep in the Brain.

Credentials and generated machine state belong in their dedicated runtime or
credential locations outside this human workspace. That separation protects a
clean, portable Brain; it does not limit ordinary agent activity.
